  "_about": "a red panda SCULPTED on its rig (2026-11-06, 2nd pass; gen: scratchpad sc/new6/redpanda.py): 55 cm of soft, fluffy, rusty-red tree-dweller -- a short stocky round-backed body, the rump a little high, on short black legs, the belly and chest black too; a big broad ROUND head with a short pointed muzzle; big round-tipped triangular ears out to the sides, white-rimmed; dark eyes; a red-brown 'tear' from each eye down to the mouth's corner, white brows, cheeks and muzzle (paints, each its own patch) to a black nose; a thick bushy tail ringed red and buff to a dark tip. Woodland; shy SHARP PASS 2 (2026-11-08): the pointed parts -- claw (3 in all) -- are the engine's sharp `horn`s (sharp.js), made from the field shapes they replaced by tools/creaturegen/sharp/ (claws.py, teeth.py, spikes.py, antlers.py, bills.py): rooted in the body, tips pointed; RE-RUN those after this species' generator. (2026-11-08, review.py: claws) The claws RE-ROOTED (review.py): each a sheath as wide as the claw where it leaves the toe, sunk in it, the join faired (horn `fair`: grown out of the skin in its paint), darker at the base fading to its own colour at the point -- no pale cut edge where it leaves the fur. (2026-11-08, ears2.py) The EARS (ears2.py): big rounded-triangular cupped sheets (sharp.js `fin`), white-furred in the hollow and round the edge, dark behind; the roots faired. WHISKERS (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sharp/whiskers.py): 9 white whiskers a side, 3 rows on the whisker pad (40-55 mm) -- `whiskers` shapes (bodyspec.js whiskerStrands: thin pointed strands, mirrored, on the head, near mesh only; details, so every coat and variant still shares one mesh).",
